  <data name="Guide.ResetTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>RESET THE REMOTE</value></data>
  <data name="Guide.Reset1" xml:space="preserve"><value>Place the remote close to the PC (a few centimetres).</value></data>
  <data name="Guide.Reset2" xml:space="preserve"><value>Hold TV + Volume − together, as shown by the pulsing circles.</value></data>
  <data name="Guide.Reset3" xml:space="preserve"><value>Release after about 5 seconds: the remote forgets its pairing.</value></data>
  <data name="Guide.Reset4" xml:space="preserve"><value>If it does not respond, plug it into its Lightning cable for 30 minutes and try again.</value></data>
  <data name="Guide.Hold" xml:space="preserve"><value>Hold for about 5 seconds</value></data>
  <data name="Guide.PairTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>PUT IT IN PAIRING MODE</value></data>
  <data name="Guide.Pair1" xml:space="preserve"><value>In Settings, click “Pair (Bluetooth)…”.</value></data>
  <data name="Guide.Pair2" xml:space="preserve"><value>Hold Menu + Volume + together, as shown by the pulsing circles.</value></data>
  <data name="Guide.Pair3" xml:space="preserve"><value>Release after about 5 seconds: the app detects the remote and connects to it.</value></data>
  <data name="Guide.Pair4" xml:space="preserve"><value>Right after pairing, one or two disconnections are normal.</value></data>
