  <data name="Driver.InstallAsk" xml:space="preserve"><value>Install WinUSB on the Bluetooth adapter?

Windows will no longer be able to use it (no Bluetooth mouse/headset) until the original driver is restored. A self-signed certificate will be added to this computer's trusted authorities (like Zadig). An administrator confirmation (UAC) will appear.</value></data>
  <data name="Driver.RestoreAsk" xml:space="preserve"><value>Restore the original driver of the Bluetooth adapter?

The WinUSB driver is removed and Windows takes the adapter back (direct Bluetooth stops). An administrator confirmation (UAC) will appear.</value></data>
  <data name="Driver.FilterInstallAsk" xml:space="preserve"><value>Install the Bluetooth filter (AppleRemoteDriver) under the adapter driver?

Experimental kernel driver: requires test-signing mode, and a bug can cause a blue screen. The adapter must be on its original driver (not WinUSB). An administrator confirmation (UAC) will appear.</value></data>
  <data name="Driver.FilterRemoveAsk" xml:space="preserve"><value>Remove the Bluetooth filter (AppleRemoteDriver) from the adapter?

